{"v":2,"s":"p","w":9,"steps":[{"t":"read","h":"Work and power","b":"<p><b>Work</b> (rad) is done when a force moves a body along its direction:</p><div class=\"fx\">A = F · s   [J]</div><p><b>Power</b> (snaga) is how fast work is done:</p><div class=\"fx\">P = A / t   [W]</div><p>Electricity bills use kWh: 1 kWh = 3.6 · 10⁶ J.</p>"},{"t":"read","h":"Energy","b":"<p><b>Energy</b> (energija) is the ability to do work.</p><div class=\"fx\">E<sub>k</sub> = m·v²/2   E<sub>p</sub> = m·g·h</div><p>Doubling the speed makes the kinetic energy 4 times bigger. Energy changes form but the total stays the same — more on this in week 15.</p><div class=\"callout\">A phone battery: energy is what’s stored, power is how fast it drains.</div><figure class=\"fig\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 320 142\" text-anchor=\"middle\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Energy changes form: at the top it’s potential (Ep = mgh), at the bottom kinetic (Ek = mv²/2). Without friction the total stays the same.\"><defs><marker id=\"ah\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" class=\"ink\"/></marker><marker id=\"ahc\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" class=\"a\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M20 30 Q120 130 300 130\" class=\"k\"/><circle cx=\"28\" cy=\"28\" r=\"9\" class=\"a\"/><circle cx=\"286\" cy=\"122\" r=\"9\" class=\"a\"/><line x1=\"296\" y1=\"122\" x2=\"316\" y2=\"122\" class=\"kc\" marker-end=\"url(#ahc)\"/><rect x=\"40\" y=\"60\" width=\"14\" height=\"40\" rx=\"1\" class=\"a\"/><rect x=\"58\" y=\"96\" width=\"14\" height=\"4\" rx=\"1\" class=\"ge\"/><text x=\"56\" y=\"114\" font-size=\"9\">Ep  Ek</text><rect x=\"220\" y=\"96\" width=\"14\" height=\"4\" rx=\"1\" class=\"a\"/><rect x=\"238\" y=\"60\" width=\"14\" height=\"40\" rx=\"1\" class=\"ge\"/><text x=\"236\" y=\"80\" ></text><text x=\"236\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"9\">Ep  Ek</text></svg><figcaption>Energy changes form: at the top it’s potential (Ep = mgh), at the bottom kinetic (Ek = mv²/2). Without friction the total stays the same.</figcaption></figure>"},{"t":"ex","q":"A 60 kg person climbs 3 m of stairs in 4 s (g = 10). Work and power?","s":["A = mgh = 60 · 10 · 3 = 1800 J.","P = 1800 / 4 = 450 W."],"a":"1800 J, 450 W"},{"t":"num","q":"Work of a 50 N force over 4 m?","a":200,"u":"J","e":"F·s."},{"t":"num","q":"600 J of work in 3 s. Power?","a":200,"u":"W","e":"A/t."},{"t":"num","q":"Kinetic energy of 1000 kg at 10 m/s?","a":50000,"u":"J","e":"1000 · 100/2."},{"t":"num","q":"Potential energy of 2 kg at 5 m (g = 10)?","a":100,"u":"J","e":"mgh."},{"t":"mc","q":"If speed doubles, kinetic energy becomes:","o":["2× larger","4× larger","the same","half"],"a":1,"e":"v² → (2v)² = 4v²."}]}